      "curator_notes": "Real, protocol-matched quantitative metric (2026-09-23): Thermal Enhancement Ratio (TER) = 3.8 at 42 degC in RKO, as directly reported by Helderman et al. 2020 (main text: 'TER ratios of 2.5, 3.8, and 7.2 at 41, 42, and 43 degC, respectively'). TER = IC50(37 degC) / IC50(hyperthermia) -- a real literature-reported synergy metric, NOT a Bliss/Loewe/HSA/ZIP score from synlethality/scoring.py (no raw dose x temperature viability matrix was accessible; the paper's own full supplementary PDF is blocked by MDPI's bot protection from every access path tried -- direct fetch, WebFetch, and PMC's own supplementary mirror all 403/404). Cisplatin (TER=3.5) and oxaliplatin (TER=3.3) also have real TER values in this paper, but only at 43 degC, not the exact 42 degC this modifier specifies -- left as combined_effect_metric=None rather than assign a value from a different condition than what's actually modeled here.",
